# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this guide, we will show how to choose subspace dimensions in the `qiskit_addon_sqd` package to post-process quantum samples using the [self-consistent configuration recovery technique](https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.05068).\n"
msgstr "Dalam panduan ini, kami akan menunjukkan cara memilih dimensi subruang dalam pakej `qiskit_addon_sqd` untuk memproses pasca sampel kuantum menggunakan [teknik pemulihan konfigurasi konsisten-kendiri](https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.05068).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "More importantly, this guide also highlights some differences in the behavior in the subspace construction when run in `open_shell = False` or `open_shell = True` modes:\n"
msgstr "Lebih penting lagi, panduan ini juga menonjolkan beberapa perbezaan dalam tingkah laku pembinaan subruang apabila dijalankan dalam mod `open_shell = False` atau `open_shell = True`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`open_shell = False` only works when the number of spin-up and spin-down electrons is the same.\n"
msgstr "`open_shell = False` hanya berfungsi apabila bilangan elektron spin-atas dan spin-bawah adalah sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`open_shell = True` must be used when the number of spin-up and spin-down electrons is different. It can also be used when the number of spin-up and spin-down electrons is the same. However, in this last case, there is a difference in the sizes of the subspaces generated between `open_shell = False` and `open_shell = True`, as discussed in this guide.\n"
msgstr "`open_shell = True` mesti digunakan apabila bilangan elektron spin-atas dan spin-bawah berbeza. Ia juga boleh digunakan apabila bilangan elektron spin-atas dan spin-bawah adalah sama. Namun, dalam kes terakhir ini, terdapat perbezaan saiz subruang yang dijana antara `open_shell = False` dan `open_shell = True`, seperti yang dibincangkan dalam panduan ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**NOTE:** Some of the electronic-configuration (bitstring) manipulations in this package have as a goal to preserve the total spin symmetry $S^2$. Standard Selected Configuration Interaction (SCI) solvers cannot impose $S^2$ conservation exactly. Consequently, they do so approximately via a Lagrange multiplier.\n"
msgstr "**NOTA:** Sebahagian manipulasi konfigurasi elektronik (rentetan bit) dalam pakej ini bertujuan memelihara simetri spin keseluruhan $S^2$. Penyelesai Interaksi Konfigurasi Terpilih (SCI) piawai tidak dapat mengenakan keabadian $S^2$ dengan tepat. Akibatnya, mereka melakukannya secara hampiran melalui pendarab Lagrange.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The choice of electronic configurations entering the eigenstate solver can also have a strong effect in the conservation of spin. For example, in a (2-electron, 2-orbital) system, one can sample the configuration $|1001\\rangle$ (having a single spin-up excitation over the RHF state $|0101\\rangle$), which is a linear combination of the open-shell singlet and triplet states, respectively $(|1001\\rangle ± |0110\\rangle) /\\sqrt{2}$. If the configuration |0110⟩ is not sampled, one can construct neither eigenfunction of total spin, leading to spin contamination or redundancy (the configuration |1001⟩ is involved in a CI calculation, but has coefficient 0 in the CI vector). Given that a single sample $|1001\\rangle$ is generated in the quantum computer, this is how the `sqd` package handles this situation:\n"
msgstr "Pilihan konfigurasi elektronik yang memasuki penyelesai keadaan eigen juga boleh memberi kesan yang kuat terhadap keabadian spin. Sebagai contoh, dalam sistem (2-elektron, 2-orbital), seseorang boleh mensampel konfigurasi $|1001\\rangle$ (yang mempunyai satu pengujaan spin-atas ke atas keadaan RHF $|0101\\rangle$), iaitu gabungan linear keadaan singlet dan triplet lapisan terbuka, masing-masing $(|1001\\rangle ± |0110\\rangle) /\\sqrt{2}$. Jika konfigurasi |0110⟩ tidak disampel, seseorang tidak dapat membina mana-mana fungsi eigen spin keseluruhan, yang membawa kepada pencemaran spin atau lewahan (konfigurasi |1001⟩ terlibat dalam pengiraan CI, tetapi mempunyai pekali 0 dalam vektor CI). Memandangkan satu sampel $|1001\\rangle$ dijana dalam komputer kuantum, beginilah pakej `sqd` mengendalikan situasi ini:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`open_shell = False`:\n"
msgstr "`open_shell = False`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '    1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The $1001$ bitstring is split in half, representing spin-up and spin-down configurations: $10$ (up) and $01$ (down).\n"
msgstr "Rentetan bit $1001$ dibahagi dua, mewakili konfigurasi spin-atas dan spin-bawah: $10$ (atas) dan $01$ (bawah).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '    2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The list of unique spin-polarized configurations is constructed: $\\mathcal{U} = [01, 10]$.\n"
msgstr "Senarai konfigurasi berkutub spin yang unik dibina: $\\mathcal{U} = [01, 10]$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '    3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "We then consider all possible combinations of $\\mathcal{U}$ elements to form the basis: $\\left \\{ |0101\\rangle, |0110\\rangle , |1001\\rangle , |1010\\rangle \\right \\}$, which contains the singlet and triplet states.\n"
msgstr "Kemudian kami mempertimbangkan semua kombinasi yang mungkin bagi unsur $\\mathcal{U}$ untuk membentuk asas: $\\left \\{ |0101\\rangle, |0110\\rangle , |1001\\rangle , |1010\\rangle \\right \\}$, yang mengandungi keadaan singlet dan triplet.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`open_shell = True`:\n"
msgstr "`open_shell = True`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '    1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Contrary to the `open_shell = False` case, we do not combine the halves of the bitstring to form the basis.\n"
msgstr "Bertentangan dengan kes `open_shell = False`, kami tidak menggabungkan separuh rentetan bit untuk membentuk asas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Closed-shell {#closed-shell}"
msgstr "Lapisan tertutup {#closed-shell}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This example shows how the bitstrings are manipulated in a (2-electron, 4-orbital) system.\n"
msgstr "Contoh ini menunjukkan cara rentetan bit dimanipulasi dalam sistem (2-elektron, 4-orbital).\n"

